//
// CJ, 2026-11-21: "big eventuse stand or 立牌 or雕像 whatever you pick and be interactive i can click into and
// see the history or information and picture people left".
//
// ── How a district page uses it (the whole integration) ──────────────────────────────────────
//   Script tags, in this order, before the page's own script:
//     <script src="../three.min.js"></script> <script src="../GLTFLoader.js"></script> <script src="../meshopt_decoder.js"></script>
//     <script src="../memories-config.js"></script>
//     <script src="hero.js"></script> <script src="engine.js"></script>
//     <script src="photo-topics.js"></script> <script src="photowall.js"></script>
//     <script src="place-data.js"></script>            <!-- window.PLACE_DATA, generated by tools/places/build_data.py -->
//     <script src="places.js"></script>
//   Inside ENGINE.create({ build(E, models) { ... } }):
//     const D = PLACE_DATA.dadao, P = k => PLACES.item('dadao', k);
//     PLACES.add(E, P('new-year-goods-street'), { type: 'board', position: [3, 12], rotation: Math.PI / 2 });   // a marker the module builds
//     PLACES.add(E, P('xiahai-city-god-temple'), { target: templeGroup, plaque: { position: [6.4, 1.4, -4.2], rotation: 0 } });   // a building the page built
//     PLACES.mount(E, { district: 'dadao' });           // once, after the adds (adds made later still work)
//   In the page's clamp(p): PHOTOWALL.keepOut(p) already keeps her out of every marker's footprint.
//
// ── PLACES.add(E, item, options) -> entry ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//   item      an item of PLACE_DATA (or its key as a string, with options.district)
//   type      'stand' | 'board' | 'statue' | 'wall': the marker to build. Left out: the item's own marker.type
//             (events carry one), or 'board'. With `target` and no `type`, nothing is built.
//   position  [x, z] or [x, y, z] in metres · rotation  the angle about Y the front looks along (0 looks toward +Z)
//   shape     the pictogram / bronze of the marker: climber, crane, train, firework, tower, damper, stone, parade,
//             cinema, walk, bag, mask, book, lantern, fire, neon, generic. Left out: the item's marker.shape.
//   target    an existing Object3D (or an array of them): a click anywhere on it opens the item
//   plaque    with a target: { position: [x, y, z], rotation, size } hangs a glowing "i" plaque there
//   near      [x, z]: where she must stand (within `radius`, default 3 m) for the E prompt. Left out: the marker,
//             or the edge of the target's box.
//   scale     the built marker's size (default 1) · solid  false: she can walk through it
//   Calling add() twice for the same item joins the two (a statue AND the building behind it both open it).
// ── PLACES.mount(E, { district }) -> window.__places ─────────────────────────────────────────
//   Wires the click / tap, the E key and its floating prompt, the panel, and ?place=<key>.
// ── The marker builders, for a page that wants one without registering it ────────────────────
//   PLACES.stand(E, item, { shape, accent }) · PLACES.board(...) · PLACES.statue(...) · PLACES.wall(...) -> THREE.Group
//   (front looks along +Z, origin on the ground) · PLACES.plaque(E, size) -> the glowing "i" on its own
// ── Photos ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//   Each item keeps its photos under the topic 'place:<district>:<key>' through PHOTOWALL.shelf(): the same
